# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO line-ending conversion anywhere. This is deliberate and load-bearing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# freeze_manifest.json records the SHA-256 of every tracked file, and
# scripts/freeze.py --verify re-hashes the working tree against it. Any
# checkout-time rewriting of bytes makes that check fail -- not for a real
# reason, but because git handed the verifier different bytes than were
# committed.
#
# That is not hypothetical here. Python's csv module writes CRLF, so 67 of the
# derived tables and predictor score files are genuinely CRLF on disk and were
# hashed that way. The first draft of this file said `* text=auto eol=lf`,
# which would have silently converted every one of them on clone and broken
# verification for every person who cloned the repository, while verifying
# perfectly on the machine that wrote it. `-text` is what keeps the manifest
# true on someone else's machine.
#
# Do not "tidy" this into eol=lf without re-freezing.
* -text

# Explicitly binary: no diff, no conversion.
*.pt    binary
*.gz    binary
*.bz2   binary
*.tar   binary
*.pdf   binary

